    "q_en": "A person spends 40% of his income on goods for daily use, 20% of his income on house rent, 22% of his income on children’s education and 10% of the remaining on travel. Only ₹4,536 is left with him after all the expenses. What is his monthly income?",
    "q_hi": "एक व्यक्ति अपनी आय का 40% दैनिक उपयोग की वस्तुओं पर, 20% घर के किराए पर, 22% बच्चों की शिक्षा पर और शेष का 10% यात्रा पर खर्च करता है। सभी खर्चों के बाद उसके पास केवल ₹4,536 बचते हैं। उसकी मासिक आय क्या है?",
    "section": "Arithmetic",
    "solution": "1. Total percentage spent on goods, rent, and education = 40% + 20% + 22% = 82%.\n2. Remaining income = 100% - 82% = 18%.\n3. Amount spent on travel = 10% of 18% = 1.8%.\n4. Final percentage left = 18% - 1.8% = 16.2%.\n5. Given, 16.2% of Income = ₹4,536.\n6. Total Income = (4536 / 16.2) × 100 = ₹28,000.<br><br>1. वस्तुओं, किराए और शिक्षा पर कुल खर्च = 40% + 20% + 22% = 82%.\n2. शेष आय = 100% - 82% = 18%.\n3. यात्रा पर खर्च = 18% का 10% = 1.8%.\n4. अंतिम शेष प्रतिशत = 18% - 1.8% = 16.2%.\n5. दिया गया है, आय का 16.2% = ₹4,536.\n6. कुल आय = (4536 / 16.2) × 100 = ₹28,000.<br><br><b>Short Trick:</b> Remaining = 18%. After travel (90% of remaining) = 18 × 0.9 = 16.2%. 16.2% ⇒ 4536. 100% ⇒ 28000.",
    "topic": "Income and Expenditure"
  },
